# Build outputs of the local render; the grader writes to /output.
# v4: the world map is hand-written coastline polygons in lon/lat
# (composer.py CONTINENTS_LONLAT), projected equirectangular; the
# thirteen generated press photographs live in assets/ (photo-*.webp
# plus photos.json with their prompts).
# assets/entry.png is the prebuilt v5 page for the fallback path.
# v5: lead bodies shortened to end on a full stop (blind-test fix),
# #6 headline "hit" to match "capsized", grid thumbnails 52 px tall.
# v6: the map is the recolored NASA Blue Marble (assets/world-map.png,
# built by tools/recolor_map.py); grid thumbnails 58 px tall, darkest
# grid photos gamma-lifted by tools/brighten_grid.py. The raw NASA
# source image stays out of the repo (downloaded to /tmp only).
out/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
